{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftdatabase\/securityandperformance"]}],"metadata":{"role":"collectionGroup","roleHeading":"API Collection","title":"Security & Performance in SwiftDatabase","modules":[{"name":"SwiftDatabase"}]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"High-throughput SQLite column-buffered ingestion and modern SCRAM-SHA-256 password authentication for PostgreSQL."}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"SQLite Performance","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftDatabase\/documentation\/SwiftDatabase\/SQLiteConnection"],"anchor":"SQLite-Performance"},{"title":"PostgreSQL Security","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftDatabase\/documentation\/SwiftDatabase\/PostgreSQLConnection"],"anchor":"PostgreSQL-Security"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftDatabase\/documentation\/SwiftDatabase"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides & Tutorials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftDatabase\/documentation\/SwiftDatabase\/DatabaseConnectors","doc:\/\/SwiftDatabase\/documentation\/SwiftDatabase\/HighThroughputIngestion","doc:\/\/SwiftDatabase\/documentation\/SwiftDatabase\/TypeSystem"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Guides--Tutorials"}],"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftDatabase\/documentation\/SwiftDatabase\/SecurityAndPerformance","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"As datasets grow into the millions of rows and production PostgreSQL deployments enforce stronger authentication policies, ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiftDatabase","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" provides two complementary enhancements:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1024-row column buffering"}]},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"code":"SQLiteConnection.e